WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.421 --> 00:00:03.849
- [Group] Black lives
matter, black lives matter!

00:00:03.849 --> 00:00:07.140
- [Group] No peace, prosecute the police!

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.760
- [Group] Black lives matter!

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.700
- Around the world, since this weekend,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.960
there have been protests
that mixed sympathy

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.960
with the U.S. protesters
and anger at the U.S.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.340
as well as anger over local issues

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.290
in places where people see
parallels to the situation

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.400
in the U.S. that minorities
are being repressed,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.400
that police are restricting
gatherings, protests

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.820
with what they see as excessive violence.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.520
- [Woman] It's just gut-wrenching,

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.670
the climate of what's
happening in America,

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.170
and it's also happening here in Australia

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.120
though it's subtle.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.292
Racism is real for me.
(muffled group shouting)

00:00:56.292 --> 00:00:58.660
- [Group] The people, we the people!

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:02.180
- In essence, the U.S.
protests have struck a chord

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.337
in many other countries around the world.

00:01:04.337 --> 00:01:08.587
(dramatic mallet percussion music)

00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:11.506
- [Man] Say his name!

00:01:11.506 --> 00:01:12.499
- [Group] George Floyd!

00:01:12.499 --> 00:01:13.448
- [Man] Say his name!

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:14.527
- [Group] George Floyd!

00:01:14.527 --> 00:01:17.718
- [Group] No justice,
no peace, no justice!

00:01:17.718 --> 00:01:20.218
- [Group] Silence is betrayal!

00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:23.078
Silence is betrayal!

00:01:23.078 --> 00:01:25.537
(dramatic mallet percussion music)

00:01:25.537 --> 00:01:30.537
- For many years, the U.S. has
been the world's moral voice

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.800
on so many of these issues.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.800
When other countries have
called out the riot police,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.390
started bashing heads,
using water cannons,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:46.390
rubber bullets, tear gas,
the U.S. has been there

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:48.570
urging calm, wagging a finger.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.390
Russia, China, in this
case, they get to say,

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:54.610
well, look, you're doing the
same thing, United States,

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:58.500
so you have no authority to criticize us

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.693
for doing exactly what you're doing.

00:02:00.693 --> 00:02:05.693
(dramatic mallet percussion
and electronic music)

00:02:11.493 --> 00:02:15.743
(Carrie speaking foreign language)

00:02:30.892 --> 00:02:35.059
(muffled foreign language speech)

00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:41.916
(Zhao speaking foreign language)

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:53.915
- The American people.
(dramatic electronic music)

00:02:53.915 --> 00:02:55.764
The world has got hurt--

00:02:55.764 --> 00:02:59.490
(dramatic electronic music)

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:02.060
- [Dan] The situation
playing out in the U.S. now

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:04.540
is at a, probably at an emotional level,

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.930
fairly disturbing to much of the world.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:11.000
To see the U.S. literally
in flames like this

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.000
and in conflict like this
has got to be traumatic.

00:03:17.544 --> 00:03:22.544
(muffled group murmuring)
(gunfire popping)

